 filename←{parms}CreateSingleDocFromMarkdownFiles path;F;A;p;list;parms2;filename_;md;html
⍝ Collects all markdown files in path/ and compiles them into a single HTML document.
⍝ This can be useful for proof-readinging.
⍝ Note that sub folders in path\ are scanned as well.
⍝ If no ⍺ is specified a temp filename is created.
⍝ You may create a namespace and populate it with 0 to all of:
⍝  * `recurse` (defaults to 1)
⍝  * `filename (defaults to a temp filename)
⍝  * `extension` (defaults to ".md")
⍝ Returns either the name of the HTML file created of an empty vector in case no Markdown files were found
 F←##.FilesAndDirs ⋄ A←##.APLTreeUtils2 ⋄ F.APLTreeUtils2←A
 '⍵ must point to a directory'Assert F.IsDir path
 parms←{0<⎕NC ⍵:⍎⍵ ⋄ ''}'parms'
 p←⎕NS parms
 :If 0=p.⎕NC'filename'
     filename←'html'F.GetTempFilename2''
 :EndIf
 :If 0=p.⎕NC'recurse'
     p.recurse←1
 :EndIf
 :If 0=p.⎕NC'extension'
     p.extension←'md'
 :EndIf
 parms2←⎕NS''
 parms2.recurse←p.recurse
 list←parms F.ListFiles2 path,'/*',p.extension
 :If 0<≢list
     html←'<!DOCTYPE html' '<html>' '<head>' '<style>'
     html,←'@media print {' '@page {' 'size: A4;' 'margin: 2cm;' '}' 'h2 {' 'break-before: page;' '}' 'h2:first-of-type {' 'break-before: auto;' '}' '}'
     html,←'</style>' '</head>' '<body>'('<h1>All markdown files in ',path,'</h1>')
     :For filename_ :In list
         html,←⊂'<h2>Filename: ',filename_,'</h2>'
         :If 0<≢md←⊃⎕NGET filename_ 1
             html,←(⊂'<pre><code>'),md,⊂'</code></pre>'
         :EndIf
     :EndFor
     html,←'</body>' '</html>'
     (⊂html)⎕NPUT filename 1
 :Else
     filename←''
 :EndIf
⍝Done⍝
